cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TEfastR, please cite it using the metadata below, and also cite
  TEtranscripts (see references).
title: "TEfastR: fast, vectorized gene and transposable element read counting in R"
abstract: >-
  TEfastR is a vectorized, Bioconductor-based reimplementation of the
  read-counting stage of TEtranscripts. It counts reads in a BAM file against
  gene and transposable element (TE) annotations using bulk GenomicRanges
  overlaps, redistributes multi-mapped reads across TE instances with a
  sparse-matrix SQUAREM EM algorithm, and reports gene, TE element and
  per-locus TE counts with genomic coordinates.
type: software
